    "body": "That's right, both (1) and (2) support a top-level A.com prefetching B.com, to be used for an iframe that is nested under A.com.\r\n\r\nAnd just to be clear, I am not recommending that we should consider supporting prefetching in one context at some level in the tree structure, and reuse by another context at another level in the tree structure. It's just that if the fetching-and-reusing context are nested at all, we begin relying on the implementation-defined parts of the network partition key, and therefore behavior would differ depending on whether or not a browser implements double-key caching, triple-key caching, and so on, compared to browsers that don't.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
