    "created_at": "2022-01-20T23:38:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-01-20T23:38:14Z",
    "body": "We could let people be explicit about what they want via an `origin` option. So: `<link rel=prefetch as=script origin=\"https://site.example\"  href=\"https://cdn.example/some/script.js\">` would be a hint to the browser that some page on `https://site.example` is going to want `https://cdn.example/some/script.js`.\r\n\r\nThis would mean we would not need `as=document` vs `as=iframe`: they would both just use `document` with different values for the `origin` attribute.\r\n\r\nIn the case where the `origin` attribute was not provided, we could just maintain current behavior.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
