    "updated_at": "2025-03-12T05:58:31Z",
    "body": "I think we can close this issue. Since it was opened, @noamr has done the great work of fully specifying `<link rel=prefetch>`, such that it behaves like a low-priority `fetch()` and just populates the HTTP cache. This means it's not very suitable for prefetching documents, due to modern HTTP cache partitioning.\n\nChromium still, unfortunately, has some nonstandard behavior behind the nonstandard `as=document` value, but we're hoping to remove that: https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40857729.\n\nFor navigational prefetching (and prerendering), Chromium provides the technologies in https://github.com/WICG/nav-speculation, which we're discussing the process of upstreaming at https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11123. Relevant to some of the discussions above, they have various protections built in to prevent cross-site information leaks.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
